      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61af28116b1f36339f75bc78|full_name} Well, I wouldn't say that\n\nThe iOS version exists now, Silicon Macs can natively run iOS/iPad apps. That's enabled by default, but VRC has turned this off. Hopefully that sees some traction, though.\n\nAs for Desktop, virtualization-wise the M3 and upwards now has nested virtualization, which is the core component needed for VBS. VMWare and Parallels just need to integrate that support into their software, and we're good to go.",
