      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello!  I decided to Test VRChat on a Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 3x 15 running a fully updated Windows 11 installation.  Although it clears the Easy Anti cheats checks, it does not load the game itself sadly.  From Testing I was able to get the computer to run Resonite and even in VR, but VRChat does not even start.  I have collected a log and some hopefully helpful screenshots.  Feel free to reach out for any other info that you may need.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-08-12T21:12:04.654Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Epic Games just released Windows for ARM support for Epic Online Services (therefore Easy Anti Cheat) :\n\nhttps://dev.epicgames.com/docs/epic-online-services/whats-new#eos-11713-cl44532354--2025-aug-12\n\nVRChat was already running great with Prism emulation on ARM devices. Would it be possible to add that support on VRChat so people with ARM devices (like with the Snapdragon X series chips) can play ?",
